{"study_accession":"PRJNA599020","secondary_study_accession":"SRP239495","title":"RNA-Seq of human whole blood: Evaluation of globin RNA depletion on Ribo-Zero library method","description":"Peripheral blood is a highly accessible biofluid providing a rich source of information about human physiology and health status. However, for studies of the blood transcriptome with RNA sequencing (RNA-Seq) techniques, high levels of hemoglobin mRNAs (hgRNA) present in blood can occupy valuable sequencing space, impacting detection and quantification of non-hgRNAs. In this study, we evaluated two methods for preparing ribosomal RNA (rRNA)-depleted sequencing libraries for RNA-Seq of whole blood, one of which is also designed to deplete hgRNAs. Two experiments were performed: one evaluating library performance across 6 human blood samples and the other examining library reproducibility and performance in a two subject subset. We find that addition of hgRNA depletion to the rRNA-depletion protocol for library preparation from blood RNA effectively reduces highly abundant hgRNA reads in RNA-Seq data but does not result in an increase in detection of differentially expressed genes (DEG).","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":45,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN13737305","study_accession":"PRJNA599020","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","description":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","sex":"female","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2020-04-14","attributes":[["isolate","C1"],["age","not applicable"],["biomaterial_provider","not applicable"],["sex","female"],["tissue","Whole Blood"],["health_state","control"],["replicate","Library Replicate 1"],["input","900ng: High RNA Input"],["Depletion_Kit","Globin-Zero Gold rRNA RemovalKit (human)"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR10828989","experiment_accession":"SRX7502401","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"RT-PCR","instrument_model":"Ill